[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3698413837","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114298#issuecomment-3698413837","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114298","id":3698413837,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ccVEN","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-30T06:18:08Z","updated_at":"2025-12-30T06:18:08Z","body":"I tested the subway scene on a laptop with Intel Xe graphics running PopOS 22.04 and found that CPU usage was consistently higher in the editor (5ms -> 6ms) but that GPU usage was consistently lower (50 ms -> 45 ms). \n\nFurther, it looks like in your screenshots you have volumetric fog enabled in 4.6, but not in 4.5. The presence of Volumetric fog can easily explain the difference in GPU performance. Its cost also scales somewhat with the number of transparent objects on screen, so that could be why you don't see a difference without transparent objects. \n\nYou need to use identical settings between versions to accurately compare performance. Before anyone spends any serious amount of time exploring this we absolutely need a proper MRP, with an emphasis on _minimal_. This sort of mistake is easy to make when you do not take the time to make an MRP and instead just rely on testing existing demos. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3698413837/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3701764559","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114298#issuecomment-3701764559","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114298","id":3701764559,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7cpHHP","user":{"login":"thedinyamum","id":92639283,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYWQMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92639283?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedinyamum","html_url":"https://github.com/thedinyamum","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedinyamum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedinyamum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedinyamum/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedinyamum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedinyamum/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedinyamum/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedinyamum/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedinyamum/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedinyamum/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-31T08:53:19Z","updated_at":"2025-12-31T08:53:50Z","body":"Both Versions use same settings, WorldEnvironment node is untouched across either version, for MRPs they use the same settings they came 